		"summary": "Over 42 million Americans rely on Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP) benefits loaded monthly onto state EBT cards between the 1st and the 28th of the month. Exact reload dates depend on your state's issuance formula—typically determined by the last digit of your case number, Social Security number, or last name—while USDA's annual October Cost-of-Living Adjustment sets the maximum allotment per household size.",
