					"body": "While SNAP is federally funded by the USDA, each state agency administers its own monthly deposit staggered window: states like Alaska, Vermont, Rhode Island, and North Dakota load all EBT cards on the 1st of the month; California (CalFresh) issues benefits between the 1st and 10th based on the last digit of your case number; Texas (Lone Star Card) staggers deposits from the 1st to the 28th; New York issues between the 1st and 9th (upstate) or over 13 staggered days (NYC); and Florida (ACCESS) deposits between the 1st and 28th using the 9th and 8th digits of your case number."
