		"summary": "A full moon occurs every 29.5 days (one synodic month) when Earth sits directly between the Sun and the Moon. When a full moon coincides with lunar perigee—the closest point in the Moon's elliptical orbit around Earth—it becomes a Supermoon, appearing up to 14% larger and 30% brighter in the night sky, especially during moonrise on the eastern horizon.",
