					"body": "Each month's full moon carries a traditional North American and European seasonal name: November's **Beaver Moon** (marking the time beavers finish fortifying their winter lodges before swamps freeze); December's **Cold Moon** (the longest-night full moon near the winter solstice, riding highest across the northern sky); January's **Wolf Moon**; February's **Snow Moon**; March's **Worm Moon**; and April's **Pink Moon**."
