		"summary": "Mercury goes into apparent retrograde motion three to four times every year for roughly three weeks at a time. Astronomically, this is an optical illusion caused by Mercury's fast 88-day orbit lapping Earth's 365-day orbit around the Sun; culturally and astrologically, millions track Mercury retrograde and its two-week 'retroshade' periods to double-check contracts, travel itineraries, and digital backups.",
