		"summary": "The IRS typically opens the annual individual tax filing season in the final week of January, issuing more than 90% of electronically filed direct deposit refunds within 21 calendar days. Under the federal PATH Act, taxpayers claiming the Earned Income Tax Credit (EITC) or Additional Child Tax Credit (ACTC) have their refunds held until mid-February, with direct deposits hitting bank accounts around February 24–28.",
